WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.535
-Welcome.
-This is such a fun show, Seth.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm digging it.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.138
-I am so happy to have you here
because obviously

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:05.939 line:92%
you have a very fast turnaround.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.675
You have to be both on TV now
when people are going to bed.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then first thing in the
morning,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're going to see you
as well.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly, I got
a quick turnaround.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.581 line:92%
-And your morning got earlier.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're now doing
the first two hours,

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.051
or in other words 7:00 to 9:00.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:18.918 line:92%
-And then you have an hour off.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's 7:00 to 9:00 with
Savannah on the "Today" show

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you're back at 10:00
with Kathie Lee.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You got it.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.525 line:92%
-And did you ever consider

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
not doing the Kathie Lee part
anymore

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.129 line:92%
once you did the 7:00 to 9:00?

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.830 line:92%
-I like -- I like that 10:00.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.098 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I like the 10:00 too.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:32.832 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You know what it is?

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's laughing
and scratching and drinking.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like not --
It's not heavy lifting.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.105 line:92%
It's a fun little hour, yeah.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, by the time
we all get in,

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.810
the "Today" show that's on TV
is the 10:00 "Today" show.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think we all look at it
lovingly wondering

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.847 line:92%
why we work at a comedy show

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're having less fun
than you guys.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.919
-By the way, we started pouring
wine on that show,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I promise you, I felt like
the suits had no clue.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one day, they just watched
our show and said,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How long has that
been going on?"

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.861 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I know, it was the best.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How did it start?

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whose idea was it
to start having wine?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.799 line:92%
-Okay, you know what happened?

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:08.301 size:84% position:42%
Chelsea Handler came on
and she had that book,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.169 line:92%
"Hello Vodka, It's Me Chelsea."

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.205
-I love -- By the way, I'm not
surprised Chelsea enabled this.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so she -- so we served
her some drinks.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Brooke Shields showed
up the next day

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was like,
"Where's mine?"

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.846 line:92%
And we go, "Where's your what?"

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:20.914 line:92%
She goes, "Where's my booze?"

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're like,
"Get her some booze,"

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, all of the sudden,
it just happened.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think --
I thought you were --

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it was illegal
to drink on the air.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought there was
some FCC violation.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
But apparently no.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- and --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:39.332
I -- Are you -- I feel like you
guys should be, if you're not,

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should be beloved by
the wine industry.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I hope you are.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I think we are.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Kathie Lee's got
a line of wine.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we do our --
our share of hocking it.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, good.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were in South Korea
for the Olympics.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How was that?

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I tell you,
it was an absolute ball.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:56.816 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We got to go to
a ton of the events.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were --
Do you guys remember when

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:04.023
the U.S. women's hockey team won
in that, like, nail-biter?

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shoot-out. Yeah.
-It was crazy.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.393 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.162 line:92%
It was -- We went to that game.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:12.031 line:92%
Roker and I were freaking out.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.166 line:92%
It was U.S. versus Canada.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.000 line:92%
It went down to the shoot-out.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.836
It was one of my favorite
moments I think at the Olympics.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was great,
and then, someone --

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.073 size:78% position:39%
A Canadian guy posted
a wonderful video.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:23.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was obviously aware
that you guys were behind him.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:23.776 line:92%
And during the shoot-out,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
he shot himself reacting to
Canada losing

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.847
while you guys were celebrating
behind him.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought he was
a very good sport.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's take a look at this fine
Canadian gentleman.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-USA! USA!

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was totally --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-But you --

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys tracked him down
and you had him on the show.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.067 line:92%
-Do you know what was funny?

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of our producers saw him
on Insta and they said,

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:51.971 line:92%
"We got to get this guy in."

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:55.775
And he came in at midnight Korea
time and was on the air with us.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.476 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He was a great sport.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-He was a great sport, yeah.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:02.015
-I would imagine, you know, I've
been to -- I've never been to --

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I guess I have been
to a Winter --

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went to Vancouver
and I went to London.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.654 line:92%
It is that spirit of everybody

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
just collectively
being in a great mood.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:13.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you go to any of the --
I heard you went to half pipe.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is that --

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I went to see Shaun White
after he nailed it.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.796 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He was unbelievable.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.497 line:92%
And Chloe Kim, those two.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:20.466
Watching those guys just fly
through the air, it's just --

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, if you could do one
thing in your life

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and feel that free.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It was the best.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
Watching Shaun win
was something.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I cry all the time
watching the Olympics.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you -- When you're actually
there working,

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you find yourself as
emotionally attached to it

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
as somebody like me who's
sitting at home like a dummy?

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.116 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Because you're not --

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to hear all
the NBC music and, like,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys are pulling my heart
strings the whole time.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I -- There is something
about a kid

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose name you don't know
before you walk in.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:48.494
And you watch their parents who
are standing right next to them.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.864
They've driven them to the rink
at 4:00 in the morning,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:52.732 line:92%
they've practiced forever,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.034 size:81% position:41%
and it comes down to,
like, this one minute.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're watching this kid's
life change,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.072 line:92%
like, in front of your eyes.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am such a crybaby
at the Olympics

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.275 line:92%
because I feel everything.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:06.079
-Yeah. My wife walked in on me
watching the Olympics and crying

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just like said, "Wha-haa,"
and went to bed.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like,
"I can't do this again."

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.152 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.420 line:92%
But you have a 1-year-old.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were away for her
for an Olympics,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is no small amount
of time.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:22.528
And how was it? Was it hard? How
did you communicate with her?

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did -- we did a bunch of
Facetime.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.866 size:84% position:42%
-Here is your beautiful
daughter, by the way.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to show a picture
while we're talking.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
There she is.
-That's Joel.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.772 line:92%
-That's Joel and your daughter.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.173 line:92%
So how did you talk to her?

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.108 line:92%
-So, we did it on Facetime.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was hoping she wouldn't
hit any milestones

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:40.179
while I was gone because that
makes you feel kind of crummy.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.481 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But my mom was with her,

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:45.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my mom kept telling her
to say mama.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:45.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Say mama.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she videotaped
Haley saying mama.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.324 size:78% position:39%
So, I was playing it
and I was so excited.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:54.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got home
and I was like, "Hey!"

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, "It's me."

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:59.999
And she pointed to my phone
and she was like, "Mama! "Mama!"

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "No, no!"

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God.
The phone is mama.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That is horrifying.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:08.574
-You look like my mama who lives
in this phone.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:13.179
So you and your boyfriend Joel,
you guys live together.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.914 line:92%
And, obviously, you are an adult

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is
a totally normal thing.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
But is it true that you were
nervous to tell your mom

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were going to move in
with your boyfriend?

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.224 line:92%
-That's so weird. I know.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:29.195
I'm 51 year-- 52 years old when
I moved in with Joel,

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.229 line:92%
which all sounds so crazy.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:34.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember getting kind of
a little pit in my stomach

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to tell my mom.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:35.802 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I know it sounds nuts,

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:39.672
but don't you always feel
like a kid around your mom?

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm like,
"Mom, he's a great guy."

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're going to move in
together."

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like,
"Oh, and no marriage? Okay."

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:47.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay. I guess that's good
for you."

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:50.283 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I know.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.484 line:92%
A grown-- I was terrified.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
But keep in mind.
We moved in, in December.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Haley came, you know,
in February.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
So everything changed in,
like, an instant.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.592 line:92%
-Yeah, that is definitely --

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:03.129
He might've thought he was
moving in with a nice lady,

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:03.830 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and then, he was like,

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.699
"Whoa, this whole thing is
a lot more than I thought."

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.901
-I think he kind of freaked out.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:12.438
-Well, he can call his mom
and tell her all about it.

